---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const gh = "https://github.com/leat-consulting";
---

<Base
  title="Demo"
  description="The public repositories behind Leat Consulting: reusable workflows, the governance that protects them, and the pull requests that built them."
>
  <h1>Demo</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Everything here is real and public. The repositories below build and protect this website, and every
    change to them arrived through a reviewed pull request.
  </p>

  <h2><a href={`${gh}/platform-workflows`}>platform-workflows</a></h2>
  <p>
    The reusable workflows: CI, security scanning, multi-architecture container builds with verified
    provenance, and verified GitHub Pages deploys. A self-test runs every workflow on each change, and
    scans a branch of deliberately planted problems to prove each scanner still catches them.
  </p>
  <ul class="ticks">
    <li>
      <a href={`${gh}/platform-workflows/pull/1`}>Pull request 1</a>: organisation governance defined as code. It was written by
      our Claude GitHub App and could not merge until a person approved it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href={`${gh}/platform-workflows/pull/2`}>Pull request 2</a>: the first version of the workflows. Its first run failed on a
      GitHub permissions rule, and the fix is in the history.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href={`${gh}/platform-workflows/releases/tag/v1.0.0`}>Release v1.0.0</a>: an immutable release that callers pin by commit.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href={`${gh}/platform-workflows/tree/main/governance`}>governance</a>: the rulesets and organisation settings, with a
      drift check and evidence that the rules bind even the owner.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2><a href={`${gh}/leat-site`}>leat-site</a></h2>
  <p>
    The source for this website. It calls the shared workflows for CI, scanning and deployment, and
    each deploy is signed and verified before it goes live.
  </p>

  <h2><a href={`${gh}/demo-app`}>demo-app</a></h2>
  <p>
    A small service being built to show the whole flow on an application: AI review catching a bug, an
    AI fix approved by a person, a pull request blocked by a security scan, and a container image checked
    before it runs.
  </p>
</Base>
